      "title": "Brazil bans online betting and casino outright via Provisional Measure 1,394; sites go dark on 6 October",
      "text": "President Lula signed Provisional Measure No. 1,394 on 25 September, prohibiting the operation, offering, intermediation and advertising of fixed-odds betting and online games nationwide, covering both federal authorisations and state-level concessions. New deposits were barred from publication; players have until 23:59 on 5 October to withdraw balances, sites and apps go offline from 6 October, operators must report balances by CPF on 7-8 October, and banks refund players between 9 and 14 October, with Caixa handling residual cases. The government granted 85 licences at BRL 30m each (BRL 2.55bn in total) and says it will neither refund them nor pay compensation. Company penalties reach BRL 2bn, and advertising and sponsorship material must come down within 10 days. Yogonet's translation of the text shows Article 14 bars banks, payment institutions and schemes including Pix from processing betting transactions, while Article 15 tells the Central Bank to build a real-time rejection system. The measure took effect immediately but needs congressional approval within 120 days to become permanent. Attorney General Jorge Messias told CNN Brasil: 'We remain completely confident and fully prepared to respond to any challenges that may arise.' IBJR warned demand will migrate to illegal operators and licensees are preparing court action. For any platform with Brazilian customers, this is now an operational wind-down with fixed dates: withdrawal surges, balance reconciliation by CPF, refund file handovers to banks and switching off marketing all land inside two weeks, while the payment-rail block in Article 14 means that even if the ban is later reversed, the cashier will be the slowest part of the stack to come back.",
