      "title": "Macau September GGR slips 1.2% to MOP 18.1bn, the weakest month of 2026 and well below analyst forecasts",
      "text": "Macau's gross gaming revenue fell to MOP 18.1bn (USD 2.24bn) in September, down 1.2% year on year and 17.5% below August, according to the Gaming Inspection and Coordination Bureau, Inside Asian Gaming reported on 1 October. It was the lowest monthly figure of 2026 so far, with IAG noting the market has 'yet to fully rebound from the challenges presented by the football World Cup in June and July'. Nine-month GGR is up 3.2% at MOP 187.1bn (USD 23.2bn). The print missed expectations badly: GGRAsia reported before the release that JP Morgan expected about MOP 19.64bn (roughly +7%) and Seaport about MOP 20.12bn (+10%). IAG said analysts 'have nevertheless been lowering their FY26 forecasts due to general softness in the market'. The figure lands as the 1-7 October Golden Week holiday begins, which will be the next test of whether visitation and junket-agent activity are recovering. The miss is a reminder of how much event-driven substitution matters in mature markets: a summer of World Cup betting appears to have pulled discretionary gaming spend away from Macau's casino floors, which is a cross-channel effect regional operators should factor into how they read their own post-tournament cohorts.",
