      "text": "EveryMatrix announced on 25 September that Danske Licens Spil, the liberalised-market subsidiary of state-majority-owned Danske Spil, is live on its casino platform technology under a long-term partnership signed in late 2025. EveryMatrix describes the integration and migration as 'one of the most complex' it has delivered, requiring custom-built work across casino platform functions, regulatory reporting, player authentication, game integrations, jackpots, lobby integrations, responsible gaming requirements and operational workflows; the launch also brings EveryMatrix's gamification and engagement tools. Co-CEO Jonas Groes said the project 'demonstrated our ability to adapt our technology to a demanding regulated market while maintaining the flexibility to support a highly customised operator environment', while Danske Licens Spil CEO Karsten Fogh Holanng said the new platform lets it deliver 'an even more entertaining and responsible gaming experience'. EveryMatrix says the past 12 months produced its largest tier-1 turnkey deals with iGaming brands and lotteries. The platform lesson is in the list of custom work: player authentication, regulatory reporting and RG requirements are where Nordic state-linked operators differentiate, and a migration that touches all of them while preserving jackpots and lobby integrations is a reference case for other lottery-owned brands weighing a move off in-house stacks.",
