    "summary": "Finland's National Police Board had received 75 licence applications by 22 September, up from 50 in June, according to Yle. Applications opened on 1 March and no licence has yet been granted. Each applicant pays a EUR 29,000 processing fee before review begins. The licensed market replaces Veikkaus' monopoly on 1 July 2027, when supervision moves to the new Finnish Supervisory Agency. Veikkaus has created two subsidiaries to compete in the open market.",
