    "expanded": "The political debate over Veikkaus' future ownership is also live. SDP party secretary Mikkel Näkkäläjärvi said 'the state has in this situation no particular strategic interest in owning a gaming company', while only the Left Alliance opposes a sale. Nikkinen summed up the appetite: 'Finland is attracting interest. After all, this is a billion-dollar pot that is being distributed here now.' A potential privatisation of the incumbent would add an M&A dimension to the market opening and could change the competitive landscape before the first licences are issued.",
